Alternative: fetch the head's run LIST once (headWorkflowRunsSafe — all runs per_page=50) and resolve run ids from that map: a check-run whose run id is ABSENT from the head's run list ⇒ 'no-run' (404-equivalent: the run no longer exists — deleted runs drop off the list); a run with conclusion cancelled ⇒ 'cancelled'. This avoids per-run API calls entirely, reuses the existing probe, matches the #1457 evidence ("run no longer exists"), and is exactly what the ticket says: "whose run_id 404s or whose run is cancelled". Absent-from-list ≈ 404. 

Edge: pagination — per_page=50 caps; a head with >50 runs could hide an old ghost's run... but for zombie detection: if the run is not in the newest 50 of the head, and the check-run is still in_progress... could false-positive a zombie for a genuinely-running old run. Extremely unlikely (50 runs one head) and the consequence is one bounded re-dispatch. Note it.

